-                     ((pdd->alloc_watch_ids >> watch_id) & 0x1);
+     owns_watch_id = pdd->alloc_watch_ids & BIT(watch_id);
      ...
  }
```
Reason: The added early bounds check (`watch_id >= MAX_WATCH_ADDRESSES`) rejects invalid IDs before any array or bit operations. Changing the parameter type to `u32` eliminates the problematic signed conversion. Using `BIT(watch_id)` replaces manual shift-and-mask, avoiding undefined behavior from negative shifts. These changes ensure that only valid `watch_id` values (0 to `MAX_WATCH_ADDRESSES-1`) are used, preventing out-of-bounds access and undefined bitwise operations.

